        "id": 115775,
        "name": "DrScott",
        "username": "DrScott",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/d/97f17d/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-08-21T23:42:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Innate abilities can be pretty much anything. &nbsp;They include Ongoing abilities (indicated with the Kirby Dot icon) like Legacy's \"Flying\", or Action abilities (indicated with the pucnhy fist icon) like his \"THOKK!\". &nbsp;The key with innate abilities is that they don't go away when you are incapacitated. &nbsp;For heroes they consist entirely of the abilities printed on the character card. &nbsp;Villains can have scenario specific innate abilities, but these have red card backs in contrast to the blue backed standard abilities.</p>",
        "post_number": 3,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:48:02.469Z",
